# Bifrost Schema

All tables are pre-declared `DomainTable` instances registered at boot. The physical schemas below are what DataFusion sees at scan time; they include system columns. The Rust record types in `wyrd-spec` (`SpanRecord`, `GenAiSpanRecord`, etc.) are the canonical source; this page documents the derived physical layout.

## Storage format

Every table is Iceberg format v3. Appends assign v3 row lineage, and
compaction preserves each row's hidden `_row_id` and
`_last_updated_sequence_number`. Those lineage columns are Iceberg metadata:
they never appear in a table schema, its fingerprint, or a query result.

## Variant columns

A `Variant` column holds an open, self-describing value. On the Arrow wire it
is the `arrow.parquet.variant` extension over a `metadata`/`value` binary
Struct, and every Variant field, including one nested in a List or Struct, must
carry that extension. A value reads back with its own type: integers stay
integers, doubles keep their IEEE meaning, strings, booleans, bytes, arrays,
and objects keep their type, and a missing key stays distinct from a key whose
value is null. Object keys are unique; when an OpenTelemetry attribute
collection repeats a key, the final occurrence is stored.

JSON input converts an integer in the signed 64-bit range to an integer, an
integer above that but within the unsigned 64-bit range to a scale-zero
decimal, and a non-integer number to a double, so every accepted integer reads
back exactly. Send a wider integer as a string. A value is refused before acknowledgement with a stable code:

| Condition | Code |
|---|---|
| Missing or foreign Variant extension | `WYRD_VALA_400_BIFROST_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE` |
| Encoded metadata plus value over 8,388,608 bytes | `WYRD_VALA_413_VARIANT_TOO_LARGE` |
| Invalid JSON or Variant encoding | `WYRD_VALA_400_VARIANT_INVALID_JSON` |
| Nesting deeper than 64 containers | `WYRD_VALA_400_VARIANT_TOO_DEEP` |
| Integer outside the signed and unsigned 64-bit ranges | `WYRD_VALA_400_VARIANT_NUMERIC_OUT_OF_RANGE` |

Query a Variant with these operators and functions:

| Expression | Result |
|---|---|
| `v -> 'key'`, `v -> n` | The Variant at an object key or array index, or null when absent |
| `v ->> 'key'`, `v ->> n` | The same value as text: a string as itself, any other value as its JSON text, null when absent or JSON null |
| `parse_json(text)` | The Variant for JSON text; invalid JSON fails with `WYRD_VALA_400_VARIANT_INVALID_JSON` |
| `try_parse_json(text)` | The same, returning null on invalid JSON |
| `to_json(v)` | The JSON text of a Variant |

Operators chain (`attributes -> 'http' ->> 'route'`), and a `->>` result casts
with ordinary SQL semantics (`(attributes ->> 'retries')::bigint`). `->` and
`->>` apply to Variant columns only; query a JSON text column as
`parse_json(column) ->> 'key'`. Struct fields use `s['field']`.

## Table namespaces

### Shared signal tables

**Namespace:** `vala.traces`, `vala.metrics`, `vala.logs`, `vala.dev`, `vala.drift`, `vala.eval`, `vala.verification`

**Partitioning:** one time transform on `wyrd_event_time`. The OpenTelemetry tables (`vala.traces.spans`, `vala.metrics.points`, `vala.logs.records`) and `vala.dev.agent_traces` partition by UTC hour. The five verification tables (`vala.drift.observations`, `vala.eval.observations`, `vala.verification.results`, `vala.drift.result_features`, `vala.eval.result_items`) partition by UTC day, so a Verification Result and its detail rows, which share one event time, never split across partitions. Bifrost has no bucket, identity, or tenant partition transform.

**Tenant isolation:** tenant-qualified physical table + per-file footer tenant proof

Each tenant writes to its own tenant-qualified physical table. Every Parquet file records its tenant in its footer, and Oracle proves it against the authenticated tenant before reading any row.

### Tenant-scoped dynamic datasets

**Namespace:** `vala.datasets.<tenant_uuid>.<name>`

**Partitioning:** the hour or day transform on `wyrd_event_time` declared at registration; hourly when the registration declares no layout

**Tenant isolation:** Physical namespace + per-file footer tenant proof

User-defined datasets for high-volume custom observability writes. Each tenant gets its own physical table namespace. Schema defined at Data Card registration.

## Common system columns (all tables)

| Column | Physical type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `run_id` | `Utf8` (nullable) | Correlation: job/experiment run |
| `card_uid` | `Utf8` (nullable) | Correlation: owning Card |
| `principal_id` | `Utf8` | Correlation: emitting principal |
| `wyrd_request_id` | `Utf8` | Admitting request identity |
| `wyrd_event_time` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` | When the observed thing happened: the caller's value, or `wyrd_ingested_at` when absent; partitions and windows the table |
| `wyrd_ingested_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` | When Wyrd accepted the batch: one PostgreSQL timestamp per batch, read at admission; never caller-supplied |

Tables registered with `CorrelationPolicy::None` (for example `vala.system.audit_log`) carry only `wyrd_event_time` and `wyrd_ingested_at`; `CorrelationPolicy::CodeAxis` tables declare their own `run_id`.

## vala.traces.spans

The sole canonical durable table for the OTLP trace signal. Its ledger lives in
`vala-bifrost-redux::tables::traces::spans::SPAN_FIELDS`; each field carries an
immutable table-local id published as `PARQUET:field_id`. Span events, span
links, resource, scope, and the promoted GenAI attributes are columns of this
table — there are no child tables.

| Column | Physical type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `trace_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(16)` | 128-bit trace ID |
| `span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` | 64-bit span ID |
| `parent_span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` nullable | Absent for root span |
| `trace_state` | `Utf8` | |
| `flags` | `Int64` | Iceberg has no unsigned integer type |
| `name` | `Utf8` | |
| `kind` | `Int32` | OTLP `SpanKind` enum value |
| `start_time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | |
| `end_time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | |
| `duration_nano` | `Int64` | `end_time_unix_nano - start_time_unix_nano` |
| `status_present` | `Bool` | Distinguishes an absent status from a present empty one |
| `status_code` | `Int32` nullable | |
| `status_message` | `Utf8` nullable | |
| `attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `events` | `List<Struct>` | **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_events_count` | `Int64` | |
| `links` | `List<Struct>` | **payload-gated** |
| `dropped_links_count` | `Int64` | |
| `resource_present` | `Bool` | |
| `resource_attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `resource_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `resource_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `resource_entity_refs` | `List<Struct>` | OTel entity references, **payload-gated** |
| `scope_present` | `Bool` | |
| `scope_name` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_version` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `scope_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `scope_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `service_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `service.name` |
| `gen_ai_operation_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_provider_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_request_model` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_conversation_id` | `Utf8` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_usage_input_tokens` | `Int64` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `gen_ai_usage_output_tokens` | `Int64` nullable | Promoted GenAI attribute |
| `service_version` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `service.version` |
| `deployment_environment` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `deployment.environment.name`, else `deployment.environment` |
| `http_request_method` | `Utf8` nullable | Span `http.request.method` |
| `http_route` | `Utf8` nullable | Span `http.route` |
| `http_response_status_code` | `Int64` nullable | Span `http.response.status_code` |
| `url_full` | `Utf8` nullable | Span `url.full` |
| `exception_type` | `Utf8` nullable | On the span's last event named `exception` |
| `exception_message` | `Utf8` nullable | On the span's last event named `exception` |
| `exception_stacktrace` | `Utf8` nullable | On the span's last event named `exception` |
| + system columns | | |

Nested `events` elements carry `time_unix_nano`, `name`, Variant `attributes`,
and `dropped_attributes_count`. Nested `links` elements carry `trace_id`,
`span_id`, `trace_state`, `flags`, Variant `attributes`, and
`dropped_attributes_count`. Both subtrees are entirely caller content and are
omitted by a metadata-only projection. Each `resource_entity_refs` element
carries `type`, `id_keys` (`List<Utf8>`), `description_keys` (`List<Utf8>`),
and `schema_url`. Each promoted column is null when its source is absent or has
another type.

## vala.metrics.points

One row is one data point of one metric; `metric_type` selects which
kind-specific columns that row owns, and every column another kind owns stays
null.

| Column | Physical type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `metric_name` | `Utf8` | |
| `description` | `Utf8` | |
| `unit` | `Utf8` | |
| `metadata` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `metric_type` | `Utf8` | Selects the kind-specific columns the row owns |
| `time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | |
| `start_time_unix_nano` | `Int64` | |
| `flags` | `Int64` | |
| `attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `int_value` | `Int64` nullable | |
| `double_value` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `aggregation_temporality` | `Int32` nullable | |
| `is_monotonic` | `Bool` nullable | |
| `histogram_count` | `Int64` nullable | |
| `histogram_sum` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `histogram_min` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `histogram_max` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `bucket_counts` | `List<Int64>` nullable | |
| `explicit_bounds` | `List<Float64>` nullable | |
| `exponential_scale` | `Int32` nullable | |
| `exponential_zero_count` | `Int64` nullable | |
| `exponential_zero_threshold` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `positive_buckets` | `Struct` nullable | |
| `negative_buckets` | `Struct` nullable | |
| `summary_count` | `Int64` nullable | |
| `summary_sum` | `Float64` nullable | |
| `quantile_values` | `List<Struct>` nullable | |
| `exemplars` | `List<Struct>` | **payload-gated** |
| `resource_present` | `Bool` | |
| `resource_attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `resource_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `resource_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `resource_entity_refs` | `List<Struct>` | OTel entity references, **payload-gated** |
| `scope_present` | `Bool` | |
| `scope_name` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_version` | `Utf8` | |
| `scope_attributes` | `Variant` | **payload-gated** |
| `scope_dropped_attributes_count` | `Int64` | |
| `scope_schema_url` | `Utf8` | |
| `service_name` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `service.name` |
| `service_version` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `service.version` |
| `deployment_environment` | `Utf8` nullable | Resource `deployment.environment.name`, else `deployment.environment` |
| + system columns | | |

`positive_buckets` and `negative_buckets` carry nullable `offset` (`Int32`)
and `bucket_counts` (`List<Int64>`); both read SQL null when the collection is
absent. Each `quantile_values` element carries
`quantile` and `value`. Each `exemplars` element carries `time_unix_nano`,
nullable `int_value` and `double_value`, Variant `filtered_attributes`, and
nullable `trace_id` and `span_id`. `resource_entity_refs` is as on
`vala.traces.spans`.

