## vala.drift.observations

Source type: `DriftRecordObservation`.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `record_id` | `Utf8` |
| `series` | `Utf8` |
| `num_value` | `Float64` nullable |
| `str_value` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `session_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `created_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| + system columns | |

One row per observed feature; rows from one observation share `record_id`. The
observed subject is the managed `card_uid`, so the table carries no Verifier or
binding identity.

## vala.eval.observations

One row per committed Eval input record. A committed row activates every
matching `observations_ready` binding. The observed subject is the managed
`card_uid`.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `record_id` | `Utf8` |
| `session_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `context` | `Variant`, **payload-gated** |
| `trace_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(16)` nullable |
| `span_id` | `FixedSizeBinary(8)` nullable |
| `created_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `media` | `Variant` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| + system columns | |

## vala.verification.results

Exactly one row per completed Drift or Eval Verifier run. Errored, timed-out,
and running executions have no row. The managed `run_id` is the Verifier run
and the managed `card_uid` is the Verifier Card.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `result_id` | `Utf8` |
| `implementation` | `Utf8` |
| `execution_status` | `Utf8` |
| `verdict` | `Utf8` |
| `verifier_version` | `Utf8` |
| `owner_card_uid` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `subject_card_uid` | `Utf8` |
| `binding_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `trigger_identity` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `source_record_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `window_start` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` nullable |
| `window_end` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` nullable |
| `started_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `ended_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `drift_report` | `Struct` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| `eval_summary` | `Struct` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| + system columns | |

A scored Drift result sets only `drift_report`: `method` (`Utf8`), `features`
(`Variant`, keyed by feature name), and `verdict` (`Utf8`). A scored Eval
result sets only `eval_summary`: `total_tasks`, `passed_tasks`, and
`failed_tasks` (`Int32`), `pass_rate` (`Float64`), and `duration_ms`
(`Int64`). Every field inside either Struct is nullable and reads SQL null
when its Struct is absent. A completed Drift execution that could not score
valid input sets neither. There is no `details` column.

## vala.drift.result_features

One row per scored feature of one Drift result.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `result_id` | `Utf8` |
| `owner_card_uid` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `subject_card_uid` | `Utf8` |
| `binding_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `window_start` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `window_end` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` |
| `method` | `Utf8` |
| `feature` | `Utf8` |
| `score` | `Float64` nullable |
| `threshold` | `Float64` nullable |
| `verdict` | `Utf8` |
| + system columns | |

## vala.eval.result_items

One row per executed or skipped task outcome of one Eval result. Columns that
only an executed task fills are nullable; `skip_reason` and `upstream_task_id`
are set only for a skip.

| Column | Physical type |
|---|---|
| `result_id` | `Utf8` |
| `owner_card_uid` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `subject_card_uid` | `Utf8` |
| `binding_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `source_record_id` | `Utf8` |
| `task_id` | `Utf8` |
| `outcome_kind` | `Utf8` |
| `passed` | `Bool` nullable |
| `actual` | `Variant` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| `expected` | `Variant` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| `operator` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `message` | `Utf8` nullable, **payload-gated** |
| `stage` | `Int32` nullable |
| `started_at` | `Timestamp(µs, UTC)` nullable |
| `duration_ms` | `Int64` nullable |
| `skip_reason` | `Utf8` nullable |
| `upstream_task_id` | `Utf8` nullable |
| + system columns | |

